glycin
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The native extension under ext/glycin links glycin, the GNOME sandboxed image
decoder. This gem is bindings for it and nothing else: every method it defines
calls into that crate.

  https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glycin
  Copyright 2023-2026 Sophie Herold and the glycin contributors
  Licensed under MPL-2.0 OR LGPL-2.1-or-later

glycin is weak copyleft and this gem is Apache-2.0, which is a combination the
licences allow in one direction only. Nothing of glycin is copied into this
work: the dependency is linked, and no source or comment is carried across. A
distributed binary gem does contain glycin's compiled object, so it is
distributed under glycin's own terms as well as these, and the dual offer is
what makes that workable -- LGPL-2.1-or-later section 6 permits a combined work
under other terms provided the glycin portion stays relinkable and its source
remains available at the address above.

  - MPL-2.0 is file-scoped: its obligations attach to glycin's own files, and
    MPL-2.0 section 3.3 permits distributing a larger work under other terms.
  - LGPL-2.1-or-later is the alternative offer, and is the branch that speaks
    to linking.

Either way the obligation is to glycin's files, not to this binding, and it is
discharged by pointing at the upstream repository rather than by relicensing
this gem.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
glycin-loaders
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

glycin decodes nothing in-process: each format's decoder is a separate binary,
packaged as glycin-loaders, which glycin spawns under bwrap and speaks to over
D-Bus. Those binaries are a runtime dependency of this gem and are not
distributed with it, in it, or linked into it. They are installed by the host's
package manager and carry their own licences, including the licences of the
image codecs they wrap.

  https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glycin

