On libglycin
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

libglycin is the C/GObject wrapper over the same crate, intended for consumers
that reach it through GObject introspection. It appears in no part of this
product: this binding calls the Rust API directly through magnus. A Ruby
application that would rather have GObjects should use libglycin through the
gobject-introspection gem instead of this one, and the two are not meant to be
mixed in one process.
